GoBugMiner was used to construct the GoBug dataset reported in:

Emre Can Yılmaz and Recai Oktaş,
"GoBug: A Novel Defect Dataset for the Go Programming Language,"
IEEE Access, vol. 14, pp. 55248-55266, 2026.
https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2026.3682160

The study version used a source-defined registry of target Go repositories and
their project-specific bug labels. The standalone release generalizes this
selection through YAML configuration and command-line options and adds package
metadata, provenance, validation, privacy controls, automated tests,
documentation, and deterministic reproduction infrastructure.

The GoBug dataset, machine-learning experiments, resampling, tuning,
statistical analyses, and publication-specific outputs are not distributed in
this repository.
